                    \\Gamma_{\Sigma,K}(E) \hookrightarrow \Gamma_\Sigma(E)
            %p
              of sections whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
              is inside
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+space"} Fréchet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
              with the induced
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces"} closed subspaces
            %p
              Finally, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              of smooth sections with prescribed causal support (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactlySourceCausalSupport"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+limits"} inductive limits
              of vector spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{\Sigma,K}(E)
              as above, and hence they inherit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              by forming the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+limit"} inductive limit
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            .maruku-equation
