          %p#InfinitesimalObservables
            %strong Infinitesimal observables
          %p
            The definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Observable"}
            and specifically of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalObservables"}
            uses explicit restriction to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+extremal+action"} principle of extremal action
            (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrincipleOfExtremalAction"}
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+locus"} critical locus
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+loci"} critical loci
            are often hard to handle explicitly. It helps to consider a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"}> homological resolution
            ” that is given, in good circumstances, by the corresponding “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"}> derived critical locus
            ”. These we consider in detail below in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ReducedPhaseSpace"} Reduced phase space
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
            aspect of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            to just an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of a background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
            field history:
          #LocalObservablesOnInfinitesimalNeighbourhood.num_defn
            %h6#definition_15 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
                around
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
                of background
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                field history)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialVectorBundleAsAFieldBundle"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
              is spacetime-independent (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShellForSpacetimeIndependentLagrangians"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
